        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(config): retire flat and scalar streaming keys from matrix, feishu, and qqbot",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter #105709, three channels still accepted legacy streaming spellings in their plugin-owned schemas: matrix and feishu kept the flat `chunkMode`/`blockStreaming`/`blockStreamingCoalesce` keys (plus never-read `streamMode` junk on matrix), and qqbot accepted a scalar boolean `streaming` that doubled as both a mode switch and the official C2C stream-API toggle. This left the SDK flat fallback load-bearing for bundled channels and the \"one nested streaming shape\" story incomplete inside the same unshipped release train.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- **Matrix**: nested-only schema; DSL spec with a channel-local `resolveMode` preserving matrix's `\"quiet\"` mode (the DSL gained a `TMode` generic for exactly this); `accountStreamingReplacesRoot` per its merge semantics; the flat `blockStreaming` read in the monitor moved to the shared resolver; `streamMode` (never read by the matrix runtime) is stripped with an explanatory message rather than minting a mode. Because matrix account entries are schema-open (`z.record(z.unknown())`), the monitor keeps scalar handling through the same deprecation window as the core flat fallback (noted in the streaming.ts inventory).\n- **Feishu**: nested `streaming.{mode,chunkMode,block.enabled,block.coalesce}`; the legacy boolean gated streaming cards default-on, so it migrates via the mode path (true→partial, false→off). Feishu's old plugin-only coalesce fields (`enabled/minDelayMs/maxDelayMs`) were never read by the core block-delivery path — doctor strips them so `--fix` output validates against the core `minChars/maxChars/idleMs` shape. Feishu previously had no doctor contract artifact at all; a package-root `doctor-contract-api.ts` was added so separately installed builds get the migration. Bonus fix: both feishu dispatchers now pass `accountId` to `resolveChunkMode` (named-account chunkMode was silently ignored).\n- **QQBot**: scalar `streaming` was not a pure mode alias — `true` also implied the official C2C stream API. Canonical shape is now `{mode, nativeTransport}` with `c2cStreamApi` (already `@deprecated`) renamed to the shared `nativeTransport` (slack precedent); bespoke doctor migration (qqbot has no flat delivery aliases so the DSL path doesn't apply); `/bot-streaming` writes nested shapes; the manifest JSON schema anyOf replaced with the nested object.\n- **Shared DSL hardening** (also closes latent #105709 gaps): account seeding now reproduces per-slot resolver precedence (mode/block.enabled/preview.chunk are merged-entry slots; chunkMode is account-first per `resolveChunkModeForProvider`; block.coalesce merges per field), root flat keys seed accounts that already had streaming objects, and root alias-derived modes are inherited by materialized accounts.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Every bundled channel now accepts exactly one streaming config shape; legacy spellings block startup loudly and `openclaw doctor --fix` migrates behavior-preservingly (all within the same unshipped train, so users see a single migration event).\n- The SDK flat fallback now serves only external plugin configs, warned-on with a removal date.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Per-channel determinations with file:line evidence in review artifacts (matrix \"quiet\" mode + merge semantics; feishu boolean gate at reply-dispatcher.ts:262 + dead coalesce fields vs core reader src/auto-reply/reply/block-streaming.ts; qqbot scalar dual meaning in streaming-c2c.ts/outbound-dispatch.ts).\n- Delivery-trace goldens for all three channels pass unchanged (inputs converted to nested equivalents; no golden regeneration).\n- Blacksmith Testbox: target suites 779/779 across 10 shards (lease tbx_01kxce4213626tdcq1rcmb5y52), full remote check:changed green (tbx_01kxcekm23x892b012xyd5ere1); post-rebase combined re-run green with pipefail (tbx_01kxcfsy3xz2dw6t4y1m13zsrv).\n- Autoreview (codex gpt-5.6-sol xhigh, per-commit, 8 rounds): 13 accepted findings fixed (incl. the missing feishu doctor artifact for installed builds and the DSL seeding precedence set); 2 rejected with evidence (qqbot /bot-streaming mixed-state no-op is byte-identical to shipped semantics; \"don't copy chunk/coalesce\" contradicted by mattermost's merged-entry resolution).\n\nRefs #104693, #105054, #105636, #105709. Remaining follow-ups tracked: whatsapp layered-seeding conflict gaps; monitor scalar-window deletion together with the SDK fallback removal next train.\n",
        "branch": "claude/chanref-flatkeys-matrix-feishu-qqbot",
